taylor: Heads up 1: I'm assembling a "lite" troubleshooting snippet set for the error reference: 429, request timeouts, and context-too-long. goal: tiny, copy-pasteable for apps that don't use our full SDK. looking for reviewer + someone to wire CI smoke tests.

taylor: plan: 1 short JS snippet showing Retry-After + backoff, 1 Python snippet showing prompt trim heuristic, and a 1-line note about not retrying on client 4xx errors other than 429. keep things language-portable.

jamie: happy to review. can we also show an explicit max attempts constant and a small jitter function? those always save folks from thundering retry storms.

nina: i can own the CI smoke. will reuse docs/.github/snippet-runner job and make a minimal harness that asserts snippets run without syntax errors. need the branch by end of day.

ravi: +1 on jitter. also add a brief sentence under "fallbacks" that downgrading to a smaller model can change tone/format and to add regression checks for critical prompts.

infra-bot: Reminder: ensure snippets use the public import path (packages/redwood-sdk) to avoid example churn.

jamie: quick sketch for JS (will tidy in PR):
```
// JS: 429 handling with Retry-After or backoff
const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5;
for (let attempt=1; attempt<=MAX_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
  const resp = await client.request(payload);
  if (resp.status === 200) return resp.body;
  if (resp.status === 429) {
    const ra = resp.headers.get('Retry-After');
    const wait = ra ? parseInt(ra, 10)*1000 : Math.min(1000 * 2**attempt, 10000);
    await sleep(wait + jitter());
    continue;
  }
  // don't retry on other 4xx
  throw new Error(`request failed: ${resp.status}`);
}
throw new Error('max retry attempts');
```

jamie: note: `parseInt` parse base 10 and multiply by 1000 if Retry-After is seconds.

taylor: thanks, jamie. that looks good. will abbreviate for docs length but keep essentials.

nina: for Python prompt trim pseudocode i propose this tiny loop:
```
# python: drop oldest convo pairs until tokens < limit
while tokens(payload) > token_limit and len(history) > 0:
    history.pop(0)  # drop oldest user/assistant pair
payload = build_payload(history, prompt)
```

nina: i'll include a short comment recommending using a tokenizer library for precise counting.

ravi: can we add a one-liner about when timeouts occur (network vs server) and that some transient server timeouts should be retried once? tiny guidance only.

taylor: yep. i'll add: "Retry transient 5xx/timeouts once with short backoff; prefer exponential backoff for repeated 5xx/429."

jamie: small editorial: say "do not retry on 400-499 except 429" instead of "client 4xx" for clarity.

